{"id": 28, "ts": 1782903681.507188, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I appreciate Markus\u2019s thorough outline of Candidate\u202fD\u2019s operational reliability and stress resilience. However, the additional observations we\u2019ve just gathered change the picture: D is described as \u201carrogant\u201d and a \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all,\u201d and he is also noted to have a hot temper and be regarded as a loner. Those traits raise serious doubts about his crew\u2011cooperation, professional communication, and adaptability\u2014key safety\u2011critical criteria for long\u2011haul operations.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC shows a strong positive crew dynamic: he \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d which directly addresses the cooperation requirement. He also makes correct decisions quickly, understands complicated technology, and has excellent attention skills\u2014covering decision quality, technical competence, and attention. While C does have communication difficulties and limited willingness to pursue further education, these issues appear less likely to jeopardize immediate safety than D\u2019s evident interpersonal deficits.\nGiven that long\u2011distance pilots must work closely with co\u2011pilots and cabin crew under sustained pressure, I now lean toward Candidate\u202fC as the best overall fit, balancing strong technical and decision\u2011making abilities with proven crew cooperation."}
